[Unit]
Description=Prune the always-safe class on the shared devbox: host Docker volumes, every agent box's dangling images/build cache/volumes, idle Go build cache

# On 2026-09-25 anonymous volumes left by test harnesses and removed containers had piled
# up to 308 GB on the host daemon and taken the shared disk to 91%. On 2026-09-27 another
# ~585 GB had regrown in a day, out of this job's original reach: dangling images and build
# cache inside each agent box's own daemon (a dev-slot apply leaves 25-40 GB) and the host's
# Go build cache (161 GB; Go trims only entries idle for 5 days, with no size cap).
# No -a anywhere: tagged images, named volumes and anything a container or build references
# stay. The script logs bytes reclaimed per box and fails the unit, naming the box and the
# command, if any step fails (agentbox/devbox-prune).
# install.sh does not install this unit: a host links and enables it by hand
# (agentbox/AGENTS.md).
[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=%h/.dotfiles/agentbox/devbox-prune
